# Copy to server/.env.local (git-ignored). Only HMS_* names are read from it, and a value
# already in the process environment wins. Never put a key here: name the file it is in.
#
# Easiest path: from the repo root, `npm run keys` writes .secrets/ (git-ignored, mode 600) and
# `npm run demo` / `npm run dev:sandbox` pass HMS_SECRETS_DIR and the AI settings for you.
#
# Where keys and PayPal credentials are read (sandbox.env and ai.env inside it):
# HMS_SECRETS_DIR=~/.config/paypal-hackathon
#
# AI keys: extra dotenv files to read keys from, comma-separated. Only ANTHROPIC_API_KEY,
# OPENAI_API_KEY and MODEL_API_KEY are read; `#NAME` narrows a file to that one name (the reader
# ignores every other line), for example:
# HMS_AI_KEY_FILES=/path/to/other-tool/.env#OPENAI_API_KEY
#
# Provider: auto (Anthropic if its key is found, else Meta's Muse Spark, else OpenAI, else rules
# only), anthropic, muse, openai, fake.
# HMS_AI_PROVIDER=auto
#
# OpenAI or any OpenAI-compatible Chat Completions endpoint (HMS_AI_PROVIDER=openai, key
# OPENAI_API_KEY). Defaults: https://api.openai.com/v1 and gpt-6.1-sol.
# HMS_AI_BASE_URL=https://api.openai.com/v1
# HMS_AI_MODEL=gpt-6.1-sol
#
# Other providers' models: HMS_ANTHROPIC_MODEL (default claude-opus-5-5), HMS_MUSE_MODEL
# (default muse-spark-1.3).
#
# Mode: fake runtime mode replays saved answers (no network) unless this says live.
# HMS_AI_MODE=replay
